1
00:00:04,650 --> 00:00:14,114
Frederick Douglass was born into slavery in Maryland, around the year eighteen eighteen. He never knew his exact birthday.

2
00:00:14,764 --> 00:00:27,966
As a boy in Baltimore, he was taught the alphabet by the woman of the house, until her husband forbade it. So Frederick traded bread for reading lessons, and taught himself.

3
00:00:28,616 --> 00:00:39,324
In eighteen thirty-eight, he escaped to the North and took the name Douglass. Soon he was speaking out against slavery to crowds across the country.

4
00:00:39,974 --> 00:00:49,842
In eighteen forty-five he published his life story. It became a bestseller, and carried his voice across the ocean to Britain.

5
00:00:50,492 --> 00:00:57,615
He started his own newspaper, The North Star, and he stood up for women's right to vote.

6
00:00:58,265 --> 00:01:06,548
In eighteen fifty-two he asked a whole nation a hard question: what is the Fourth of July to a person who is not free?

7
00:01:07,198 --> 00:01:15,636
During the Civil War he helped recruit Black soldiers, and he met President Lincoln to demand equal pay and fair treatment.

8
00:01:16,286 --> 00:01:26,544
After the war he fought for the right to vote, and served his country as a marshal, an official in Washington, and its representative to Haiti.

9
00:01:27,194 --> 00:01:37,927
Frederick Douglass died in eighteen ninety-five, at his home on Cedar Hill. He spent his life asking America to live up to its own words.

